  "notes": [
    "Breadcrumbs/BreadcrumbItem are their own Kind names, distinct from the generic FieldMapping/Property config pattern every other widget uses for its content — the item LIST is real sub-structure, not just a config value.",
    "PageParams:{} on each item is where in-app navigation parameters would go for a clickable crumb that jumps to another page with state; empty means a plain non-navigating label.",
    "Real ids typically use the manifest_id prefix only on a fresh single-widget add (e.g. `Button_<10-char-rand>`, `Metrics_<10-char-rand>`) — the scenario this template mints for — while built-up production pages (`all_pages_draft_20260806.json`) mostly carry the generic `Component_<rand>` id instead, and Repeater/Tab/MasterDetail/Breadcrumbs were never observed prefixed at all."
  ]
